%I A402426 #18 Nov 22 2026 09:59:59
%S A402426 11,13,23,37,349,353,557,823,1031,1109,4583,11621,13109,16001,22807,
%T A402426 24373,29927,70309
%N A402426 Primes p such that 4*p# + 1 is prime, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402426 Primes prime(n) such that A402504(n) is prime.
%C A402426 a(19) > 10^5. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402426 8+1 = 9 = 3^2, so 2 is not a term;
%e A402426 8*3+1 = 25 = 5^2, so 3 is not a term;
%e A402426 8*3*5+1 = 121 = 11^2, so 5 is not a term;
%e A402426 8*3*5*7+1 = 841 = 29^2, so 7 is not a term;
%e A402426 8*3*5*7*11+1 = 9241 is prime, so 11 is a term;
%e A402426 8*3*5*7*11*13+1 = 120121 is prime, so 13 not a term;
%e A402426 8*3*5*7*11*13*17+1 = 2042041 = 1429^2, so 17 is not a term;
%e A402426 8*3*5*7*11*13*17*19+1 = 38798761 = 103*376687, so 19 is not a term.
%o A402426 (PARI) my(P=4); forprime(p=2, 1000, P*=p; if(ispseudoprime(P+1), print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402426 Cf. A002110 (primorials), A102476 (4 times primorials), A402504.
%Y A402426 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402426 nonn,more,new
%O A402426 1,1
%A A402426 _Jianing Song_, Nov 18 2026
